'' RUN: 'function = v' of the result's own type runs its 'operator let' -- over a variable,
'' '*p', 'this', a paren-less call, a type with a constructor and a large one -- while 'return
'' v' copies; and 'y = MakeOne' (a paren-less call returning by value) builds. Expected output
'' is fbc-modern 1.20's, byte for byte.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/result-let.tiko -o tests/codegen/resultlet.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/resultlet.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/resultlet.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: alet 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: b 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: clet 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: d 5
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: elet 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: fbiglet 1006
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: g 6
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hlclet 17
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: i 7
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: jletlet 105
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: klet 103
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: letl 103
